# PTP DeviceInfo dataset, Samsung SM-S901U (Galaxy S22).
#
# Source command:
#   BSDROID_DEBUG=1 mtpprobe caps
#
# The dataset is the payload of the data phase of GetDeviceInfo, operation
# 0x1001. The dataset holds 457 bytes.
#
# The device supports 35 operations, and the list holds every operation a
# filesystem needs:
#
#   GetPartialObject     0x101b   read part of a file
#   GetPartialObject64   0x95c1   read part of a file, 64 bit offset
#   SendObjectInfo       0x100c   announce a new file
#   SendObject           0x100d   write a new file
#   SendPartialObject    0x95c2   write part of a file
#   DeleteObject         0x100b   remove a file
#   MoveObject           0x1019   move a file
#   CopyObject           0x101a   copy a file
#   SetObjectPropValue   0x9804   rename a file
#   GetObjectPropList    0x9805   read a folder in one operation
#   TruncateObject64     0x95c3   change the size of a file
#   BeginEditObject      0x95c4   change a file in place
#
# A read and write filesystem is therefore possible on this device.
#
# The first fields:
#   6400        StandardVersion = 100, which is version 1.00
#   06000000    VendorExtensionID = 6, which is Microsoft MTP
#   6400        VendorExtensionVersion = 100
#   48          a string of 72 characters, the vendor extension description
#
# After the description:
#   0000        FunctionalMode = 0
#   23000000    OperationsSupported holds 0x23 = 35 codes

